  "diagnosis_text": "**Diagnosis:** the inter-switch link from **s3 port 1 to s4 port 2 is down**.\n\nEvidence:\n- `h1 \u2192 h5` ICMP fails completely: **5/5 packets lost**.\n- ONOS topology shows the configured **s3\u2013s4** link is missing from active links.\n- `s3-eth1` (port 1), whose configured peer is `s4` port 2, is **disabled**.\n- The installed forwarding rule on s1 sends traffic for h5\u2019s MAC (`00:...:05`) toward s2, so the selected path is:\n  `h1 \u2014 s1 \u2014 s2 \u2014 s3 \u2014 s4 \u2014 s5 \u2014 h5`.\n  That path terminates at disabled `s3-eth1`.\n- The direct physical `s1\u2013s5` link and both host-facing ports are enabled, but the current flow programming does not use that link for h1\u2192h5 traffic.\n\n**Fault localisation:** `s3-eth1 \u2194 s4-eth2` (the s3\u2013s4 segment), specifically observed down at **s3 port 1**.\n\nThe next operational action is to restore/enable that link, or update the forwarding policy to route h1\u2194h5 over the active direct `s1\u2013s5` link.",
